findings.comment:
4-602.13: The following non-food contact surfaces are observed soiled:
1) The outside of the two roasters in the kitchen (soiled with food splash);
2) the outside of the bulk white powder containers (thick food splash on lids and sides);
3) shelving on the cookline (grease and flour debris);
4) hot drawer (accumulated food debris);

See violation #s 38 and 55 - the facility would benefit from a detail cleaning to avoid a pest infestation outbreak. 

NonFOOD-CONTACT SURFACES of EQUIPMENT shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to preclude accumulation of soil residues.

750.800e - Detail cleaning is needed for several general surfaces, including but not necessarily limited to, the following:
A) storage cart by fryers (grease);
B) hot holding drawers (splash along edges);
C) storage pans and containers used for various items (crumbs/debris);  and
D) dessert cooler - bottom inside (puddling water/general buildup) & tracks of doors (general debris).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
